# Work Artifact Wording

Keep commit messages, PR descriptions, release notes, and documentation focused on the technical change, user impact, and validation status.

Avoid unnecessary private workflow details in durable project artifacts, including agent assistance, conversation context, local machine quirks, or who performed which step.

Use clear validation language. Examples:

```text
Validation: local import check passed.
```

```text
Validation: not run; live source fetch requires confirmation.
```

```text
Validation pending.
```

For commit messages, use the commit-message rule. For chat summaries, be direct and practical; they do not need to follow a rigid external-facing format.
